  "sha256:8b3a2e083e627932825499b5d1cea2131e93d90f5951d7c4a65db368ff408021": "Version 4\r\nSHEET 1 1200 800\r\nWIRE 0 -32 48 -32\r\nWIRE 128 -32 160 -32\r\nWIRE 240 -32 320 -32\r\nWIRE 320 -32 368 -32\r\nWIRE 320 -32 320 16\r\nWIRE 320 80 320 128\r\nWIRE 0 16 0 -32\r\nWIRE 0 96 0 128\r\nFLAG 320 128 0\r\nFLAG 368 -32 out\r\nFLAG 0 128 0\r\nFLAG 0 -32 in\r\nSYMBOL voltage 0 0 R0\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Invisible 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName V1\r\nSYMATTR Value PULSE(0 1 0 1n 1n 1 2)\r\nSYMBOL res 144 -48 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R1\r\nSYMATTR Value 150\r\nSYMBOL ind 256 -48 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 5 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName L1\r\nSYMATTR Value 10m\r\nSYMATTR SpiceLine Rser=0\r\nSYMBOL cap 304 16 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName C1\r\nSYMATTR Value 100n\r\nTEXT 0 -224 Left 2 ;Second-order low-pass (series RLC, output on C): H(s) = ω0² / (s² + s ω0/Q + ω0²)\\nω0 = 1/√(LC) = 31.6 krad/s (f0 ≈ 5.03 kHz) and Q = √(L/C) / R ≈ 2.1: two complex poles at −ω0/2Q ± jω0√(1 − 1/4Q²).\\nStep: it overshoots (about 46 %) and rings at f0 while it settles. Bode: a peak of about Q (6.7 dB) near f0 and then −40 dB/decade; the phase goes from 0 to −180°.\r\nTEXT 0 192 Left 2 !.tran 1m\r\n",
  "sha256:8feaed3fef7087ba149e6cef4d7ca025db6df1841724b1102bba40d3f1795d92": "Version 4\r\nSHEET 1 1200 800\r\nWIRE 0 -32 48 -32\r\nWIRE 128 -32 160 -32\r\nWIRE 240 -32 320 -32\r\nWIRE 320 -32 368 -32\r\nWIRE 320 -32 320 16\r\nWIRE 320 80 320 128\r\nWIRE 0 16 0 -32\r\nWIRE 0 96 0 128\r\nFLAG 320 128 0\r\nFLAG 368 -32 out\r\nFLAG 0 128 0\r\nFLAG 0 -32 in\r\nSYMBOL voltage 0 0 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName V1\r\nSYMATTR Value AC 1\r\nSYMBOL res 144 -48 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R1\r\nSYMATTR Value 150\r\nSYMBOL ind 256 -48 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 5 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName L1\r\nSYMATTR Value 10m\r\nSYMATTR SpiceLine Rser=0\r\nSYMBOL cap 304 16 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName C1\r\nSYMATTR Value 100n\r\nTEXT 0 -224 Left 2 ;Second-order low-pass (series RLC, output on C): H(s) = ω0² / (s² + s ω0/Q + ω0²)\\nω0 = 1/√(LC) = 31.6 krad/s (f0 ≈ 5.03 kHz) and Q = √(L/C) / R ≈ 2.1: two complex poles at −ω0/2Q ± jω0√(1 − 1/4Q²).\\nStep: it overshoots (about 46 %) and rings at f0 while it settles. Bode: a peak of about Q (6.7 dB) near f0 and then −40 dB/decade; the phase goes from 0 to −180°.\r\nTEXT 0 192 Left 2 !.ac dec 100 100 100k\r\n",
