  "sha256:5ecde83b6d1ab2dae693096b8c9ea17d774902e72021126bc9ea5627bc163851": "Version 4\r\nSHEET 1 1200 800\r\nWIRE 0 -32 48 -32\r\nWIRE 128 -32 160 -32\r\nWIRE 224 -32 320 -32\r\nWIRE 320 -32 368 -32\r\nWIRE 320 -32 320 16\r\nWIRE 320 96 320 128\r\nWIRE 0 16 0 -32\r\nWIRE 0 96 0 128\r\nFLAG 320 128 0\r\nFLAG 368 -32 out\r\nFLAG 0 128 0\r\nFLAG 0 -32 in\r\nSYMBOL voltage 0 0 R0\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Invisible 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName V1\r\nSYMATTR Value PULSE(0 1 0 1n 1n 1 2)\r\nSYMBOL ind 144 -48 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 5 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName L1\r\nSYMATTR Value 10m\r\nSYMATTR SpiceLine Rser=0\r\nSYMBOL cap 224 -48 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 32 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 32 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName C1\r\nSYMATTR Value 100n\r\nSYMBOL res 304 0 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName R1\r\nSYMATTR Value 150\r\nTEXT 0 -224 Left 2 ;Second-order band-pass (series RLC, output on R): H(s) = s ω0/Q / (s² + s ω0/Q + ω0²)\\nω0 = 1/√(LC) = 31.6 krad/s (f0 ≈ 5.03 kHz) and Q = √(L/C) / R ≈ 2.1: two complex poles at −ω0/2Q ± jω0√(1 − 1/4Q²). A zero at s = 0.\\nGain 1 (0 dB) at f0 and a bandwidth f0/Q ≈ 2.4 kHz between the −3 dB points; ±20 dB/decade far from f0 and a phase from +90° to −90°.\\nStep: a damped oscillation that starts and ends at 0.\r\nTEXT 0 192 Left 2 !.tran 1m\r\n",
