  "sha256:ac1d19ea09190f4b00a6a01f4f2c28ce5103344fea2810b4ffa9f2b225ef4819": "Version 4\r\nSHEET 1 1200 800\r\nWIRE 0 -32 48 -32\r\nWIRE 128 -32 208 -32\r\nWIRE 208 -32 256 -32\r\nWIRE 208 -32 208 16\r\nWIRE 208 96 208 112\r\nWIRE 208 176 208 208\r\nWIRE 0 16 0 -32\r\nWIRE 0 96 0 128\r\nFLAG 208 208 0\r\nFLAG 256 -32 out\r\nFLAG 0 128 0\r\nFLAG 0 -32 in\r\nSYMBOL voltage 0 0 R0\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Invisible 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName V1\r\nSYMATTR Value PULSE(0 1 0 1n 1n 1 2)\r\nSYMBOL res 144 -48 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R1\r\nSYMATTR Value 150\r\nSYMBOL ind 192 0 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName L1\r\nSYMATTR Value 10m\r\nSYMATTR SpiceLine Rser=0\r\nSYMBOL cap 192 112 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName C1\r\nSYMATTR Value 100n\r\nTEXT 0 -224 Left 2 ;Second-order band-stop or notch (output on the series LC): H(s) = (s² + ω0²) / (s² + s ω0/Q + ω0²)\\nω0 = 1/√(LC) = 31.6 krad/s (f0 ≈ 5.03 kHz) and Q = √(L/C) / R ≈ 2.1: two complex poles at −ω0/2Q ± jω0√(1 − 1/4Q²).\\nThe zeros are on the jω axis, at ±jω0: at f0 the LC is a short circuit and the output is 0. Bode: 0 dB far from f0 and a deep notch at f0, where the phase jumps 180°.\\nStep: out jumps to 1 (at first L is an open circuit), dips with a damped ring and goes back to 1.\r\nTEXT 0 272 Left 2 !.tran 1m\r\n",
