  "sha256:6db3ea0e5f52ecaa21d56dc9840c6236b14ee498fdbc2c47a701f86c6cd54cf1": "Version 4\r\nSHEET 1 1200 800\r\nWIRE 0 16 0 -32\r\nWIRE 0 96 0 128\r\nWIRE 0 -32 80 -32\r\nWIRE 80 -32 112 -32\r\nWIRE 192 -32 256 -32\r\nWIRE 304 -32 256 -32\r\nWIRE 256 -32 256 -128\r\nWIRE 320 -128 256 -128\r\nWIRE 400 -128 464 -128\r\nWIRE 464 -128 464 0\r\nWIRE 416 0 464 0\r\nWIRE 464 0 512 0\r\nWIRE 80 -32 80 32\r\nWIRE 112 32 80 32\r\nWIRE 192 32 256 32\r\nWIRE 256 32 304 32\r\nWIRE 256 32 256 64\r\nWIRE 256 144 256 160\r\nWIRE 256 224 256 256\r\nFLAG 0 128 0\r\nFLAG 0 -32 in\r\nFLAG 512 0 out\r\nFLAG 256 256 0\r\nSYMBOL voltage 0 0 R0\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Invisible 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName V1\r\nSYMATTR Value PULSE(0 1 0 1n 1n 1 2)\r\nSYMBOL res 208 -48 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R2\r\nSYMATTR Value 10k\r\nSYMBOL res 416 -144 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R3\r\nSYMATTR Value 10k\r\nSYMBOL OA_NoPole 496 -48 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName U1\r\nSYMBOL res 208 16 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R1\r\nSYMATTR Value 150\r\nSYMBOL ind 240 48 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName L1\r\nSYMATTR Value 10m\r\nSYMATTR SpiceLine Rser=0\r\nSYMBOL cap 240 160 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName C1\r\nSYMATTR Value 100n\r\nTEXT 0 -352 Left 2 ;Second-order all-pass with an op amp: R1 and the series L1-C1 are a notch into the + input, and R2 = R3 make the amplifier subtract the input (U1 has no poles: only its gain):\\nout = 2·V(+) − in, that is, H(s) = V(out) / V(in) = (s² − s ω0/Q + ω0²) / (s² + s ω0/Q + ω0²) with ω0 = 1/√(LC) and Q = √(L/C) / R1 ≈ 2.1.\\n|H| = 1 at every frequency and the phase goes from 0 to −360° (−180° at f0 ≈ 5.03 kHz). The zeros are the poles mirrored on the right half-plane.\\nStep: out jumps to 1 (at first L1 is an open circuit), dips to about 0.3, rings and settles back at 1.\r\nTEXT 0 320 Left 2 !.tran 1m\r\n",
